<entry><title>Virginia Capital Trail, November 14</title><id>https://rvabikefeed.github.io/post/618cbfda14cad862</id><updated>2026-11-14T00:12:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T00:12:11Z</published><author><name>Virginia Capital Trail</name></author><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;From Virginia Capital Trail&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/2c78398e42cc1a3f.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/7e5454acc2e8e0f8.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/f881eea93539bd80.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/0ea059ecd95ffd5d.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/e42371f69511f1ee.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/388d81157049175c.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/c2b1f1b3b3da3a34.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/716c8d11b2d70c0b.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/f67be61419b87784.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/5fecaeb06c53c7e9.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;🎉 Eleven years of the Virginia Capital Trail! We have so much to celebrate and even more to look forward to! 💙💚 &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
We had a wonderful time with our Board of Directors, community partners, and fellow Trail supporters at our 2026 State of the Trail at Historic Westover on Sunday. It was a great opportunity to reflect on the Trail’s impact over the last 11 years, share how it’s inspiring trail development across Virginia, highlight the exciting progress of the Williamsburg extension, and talk about what’s coming up next! &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
We were also happy to welcome Delegate Jessica Anderson, who presented a Certificate of Resolution recognizing the Capital Trail and its contributions to the region, along with Virginia’s Director of Recreation, Heather Barrar. &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
A special thank you to our friends at Indian Fields Tavern, Cul’s Courthouse Grille, and Breez-In for generously providing food for this year’s event. We’re excited to see the Trail continue to grow and connect even more communities in the years ahead. Here’s to the next 11 years! 🏃🏿‍♂️🚴🏿‍♀️🚶‍♀️&lt;br/&gt;
