<entry><title>Virginia Capital Trail, November 9</title><id>https://rvabikefeed.github.io/post/48b81c3faf06a98b</id><updated>2026-11-09T22:52:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:52:56Z</published><author><name>Virginia Capital Trail</name></author><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;From Virginia Capital Trail&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;🌳 Help shape the future of outdoor recreation in Virginia!...&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/071e29788f6ae0be.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;🌳 Help shape the future of outdoor recreation in Virginia!&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
From the trails we ride and walk to the parks we explore and rivers we enjoy, Virginia’s outdoor spaces mean something special to all of us. 🚲⛺ Now’s your chance to help shape what comes next!&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Virginia is developing its first-ever Outdoor Recreation Strategic Plan, and Virginia’s new Director of Outdoor Recreation, Heather Barrar, wants to hear from YOU! 🗣 What do you love about Virginia’s outdoor spaces? What would make them even better? What’s still needed in your community? 🌄&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Did you know outdoor recreation contributes $14.4 billion to Virginia’s economy and supports more than 126,000 jobs? 🤩 Your input can help make sure the future of outdoor recreation reflects the needs of communities across the Commonwealth.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Please take a few minutes to complete the survey before it closes on November 18th. Every voice matters when it comes to protecting and improving the places we love. 🚶🏼‍♀️🏃🏿‍♂️🚴🏾‍♀️&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
🔗 naturalresources.virginia.gov/outdoor/virginia-outdoor-recreation-listening-tour-survey&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
🏷️ #virginiaisfortraillovers #gooutside #virginiatrails #virginiaisforoutdoorlovers #virginiaoutdoors</content></entry>
